1. Insert the pr token between the issue anchor and the leg: `teammate: <event> #<n> · pr-1591 rework`. Then `stubTailLegOf` still works (`\s(dev|review|rework)$` matches " rework"). And the issue-number token `#1591`... wait, the gate also uses '#<n>' tokens? The title is `teammate: workflow_dispatch #<issue.number || inputs.issue> ...`. For a PR-anchored fork dispatch, inputs.issue is empty, so it's `# rework` (as thread notes). Insert pr after the '#...' part.

But also `gh-944 '#<n>' tokens` guard mentioned in smAgent — there might be title guards parsing `#<n>`. Putting 'pr-1591' after the issue number shouldn't disturb `#<n>` parsing since pr-N isn't a number token.

2. Alternatively update `stubTailLegOf` regex to allow an optional trailing pr token. But that's more invasive and stubTailLegOf semantics would need care.

Option 1 keeps `legOfRunName` untouched. Suggested run-name:

