Important: `stubTailLegOf` regex `/\s(dev|review|rework)$/` — requires the title to END with the leg token. So if I append '· pr-N' after the leg, `stubTailLegOf` would break (title ends with pr-N). Thread 9's suggestion: "append `${ inputs.pr != '' && format('· pr-{0}', inputs.pr) }`, preserving the trailing-leg token `legOfRunName` parses" — hmm, it says append while preserving the trailing-leg token that legOfRunName parses. Contradiction? If we append after the leg, the leg is no longer trailing. So the pr token must be inserted BEFORE the leg token, or `stubTailLegOf`/the anchor matching must be updated.

