+// the SM's runtime cwd is the ENGINE checkout (the gh-1070 silent-update
+// comment above, live-verified: `git fetch origin` there fetched
+// dmtools-agents and every PR pathspec 404'd; the builder clones the
+// TARGET repo instead), so `origin` names the engine repo and every
+// non-self-host SM would ask the WRONG repository about the pull ref —
+// a live fork head in the target repo misclassified 'dead' (AC2
+// inverted: wrong markers, wrong park). The probe rides the established
+// split-literal token URL (validationLiveness.forkPushTokenUrl):
+// '${GH_TOKEN}' interpolates in the child env exactly like the existing
+// silent-update commands, so the secret never appears in source or the
+// captured command string — and the token URL authenticates against a
+// PRIVATE base repo, where a hardcoded public https URL answers
+// "Repository not found" and would fail open to LIVE forever, silently
+// voiding AC3 exactly where most of the fleet runs. The pull ref is
+// served by GitHub regardless of where the fork branch lives or whether
+// it still exists; empty output (ls-remote exits 0 on a missing ref)
+// means the fork is gone entirely. Fail OPEN on a probe error — a blind
+// tick never parks (the gh-922 invariant) — but log a DISTINCT DEGRADED
+// warning so a private-repo auth failure is greppable in the SM logs.
+function forkPullRefLive(repoInfo, prNumber) {
+    var ref = forkDispatchModule.pullHeadRef(prNumber);
+    var full = String(repoInfo.owner || '') + '/' + String(repoInfo.repo || '');
